---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import { tools_read_published } from "@data/tools.js";
const EMAIL = "contact@whatifbench.com";
const UPDATED = "25 September 2026";

// 이 페이지가 말하는 "계산기"는 발행된 도구의 개수를 약속한다 — 하나인데 복수형으로
// 쓰면 거짓이다. `[category].astro`의 `elsewhere_text`와 같은 규율이다: 개수에서
// 문장을 만든다. 두 번째 도구가 발행되면 문장이 저절로 복수형으로 바뀐다.
const CALCULATOR_MIN_FOR_PLURAL_TEXT = 2;
const manyCalculators = tools_read_published().length >= CALCULATOR_MIN_FOR_PLURAL_TEXT;
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="This site stores nothing itself. What Cloudflare processes to serve it, what advertising would change, and the choices you have."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="legal-date">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

  <p>
    This policy explains what happens to data when you visit whatifbench.com.
    The short version: the site has no accounts, no newsletter, and no login,
    and {manyCalculators ? "the calculators run" : "the one calculator on it runs"}{" "}
    entirely in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>What the {manyCalculators ? "calculators do" : "calculator does"} with your input</h2>

  <p>
    There is no text box to fill in: you set a calculator with buttons and
    sliders, and those settings are processed by JavaScript running on
    your own device. The calculator itself sends them nowhere. It does write the
    current settings into the page address, after the "?", so that a link
    reopens the same view. That makes them part of the address: if you reload,
    bookmark or share that address, the settings travel with it like any other
    address, and the request for that address carries them to Cloudflare, which
    serves this site. The next section describes what is processed there.
  </p>

  <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>

  <p>
    This site is served through Cloudflare, which processes technical data
    needed to deliver pages and to protect the site from abuse. This includes
    your IP address, browser and device type, the pages requested, and the time
    of the request.
  </p>

  <h2>Fonts</h2>

  <p>
    The typefaces are served from this site's own address, like every other
    file on it. No font request goes to Google or any other third party, and no
    cookie is set by this.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>

  <p>
    This site does not currently show advertising. It is intended to carry
    advertising supplied by Google, including Google AdSense, and this section
    describes what would happen once it does. From then on, third-party vendors,
    including Google, would use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits
    to this and other websites.
  </p>

  <p>
    Google's use of advertising cookies would enable it and its partners to serve
    ads to you based on your visit to this site and other sites on the internet.
    You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting{" "}
    <a
      href="https://myadcenter.google.com/"
      rel="nofollow noopener"
      target="_blank">My Ad Center</a
    >. The WebChoices tool at{" "}
    <a
      href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/"
      rel="nofollow noopener"
      target="_blank">aboutads.info</a
    > opts you out of the participating companies you tick on its list, and it
    records that choice in the browser you use it in, so it does not reach your
    other browsers or devices. The tool also points to a Protect My Choices
    browser extension, which it says protects those preferences against
    accidental deletion.
  </p>

  <p>
    Any third-party advertising vendor would operate under its own privacy
    policy. Google describes how it uses data from sites that use its services at{" "}
    <a
      href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
      rel="nofollow noopener"
      target="_blank">policies.google.com</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>

  <p>
    This site sets no cookies of its own. Cloudflare, which serves the site, may
    set cookies of its own; Cloudflare's documentation lists them, and gives the
    condition for several of them, at{" "}
    <a
      href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/fundamentals/reference/policies-compliances/cloudflare-cookies/"
      rel="nofollow noopener"
      target="_blank">developers.cloudflare.com</a
    >. No advertising cookie is set today.
  </p>

  <h2>If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom</h2>

  <p>
    Where the GDPR applies, the legal basis for processing technical data is
    legitimate interest in operating and securing the site. The legal basis for
    personalised advertising is your consent. Since the site does not yet show
    advertising, no consent notice is displayed; one will be shown, and will be
    changeable at any time, before any advertising cookie is set.
  </p>

  <p>
    This site stores nothing itself: it keeps no logs and no copy of the technical
    data described above. That data is held by Cloudflare, and how long it is kept
    is set by Cloudflare's own policy.
  </p>

  <p>
    You have the right to request access to your personal data, correction or
    deletion of it, restriction of processing, and to object to processing. Data
    portability — receiving the data you provided in a machine-readable form, and
    having it sent to another provider — applies where the processing rests on your
    consent or on a contract and is carried out by automated means. Where processing is based on consent you can withdraw it at any
    time, and you can lodge a complaint with your data protection supervisory
    authority. To exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}
    >{EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>If you are in California</h2>

  <p>
    Under the CCPA you have the right to know what personal information is
    collected, to request its deletion or correction, to opt out of its sale or
    sharing, to limit the use and disclosure of sensitive personal information,
    and not to be
    treated differently for using these rights. Sale and sharing are separate
    things in the law: a sale is a disclosure for monetary or other valuable
    consideration, while sharing is a disclosure for cross-context behavioural
    advertising — advertising targeted using your activity across other sites —
    whether or not anything is paid for it. This site does not sell personal
    information, and, showing no advertising yet, it does not share it in that
    sense either. To make a request, use the email address above.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>

  <p>
    This site is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly
    collect their personal information. Nothing here asks for it: there is no
    text box, no account and no newsletter, and this site holds no copy of the
    technical data described above to delete — that data is held by Cloudflare.
    If you believe a child's personal information has reached this site, email
    the address above, and I can take the request to Cloudflare.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>

  <p>
    Pages here may link to other sites. Those sites have their own policies and
    are outside my control.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>

  <p>
    This policy may be updated. The date at the top reflects the most recent
    revision. Material changes will be noted on this page.
  </p>

  <p>
    The revision of 25 September 2026 named the right to limit disclosure as well
    as use for California readers, added the automated-processing condition the
    portability right carries, and pointed the advertising opt-out at My Ad
    Center, which is what Google now calls that setting.
  </p>

  <p>
    The revision of 24 September 2026 described the controls a calculator
    actually has, added that settings carried in the page address reach
    Cloudflare when that address is requested again, put the advertising section
    in the conditional, said what the aboutads.info tool does and does not
    cover, answered sharing as well as sale for California readers, and said
    what can and cannot be done about a child's data given that this site keeps
    no copy of it. A later pass the same day cut the cookie section back to what
    Cloudflare's documentation states.
  </p>

  <p>
    The revision of 23 September 2026 said which cookies can be set today, added
    that this site keeps no logs of its own, and spelled out when data
    portability and withdrawal of consent apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>

  <p>
    Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>, the
    same address listed on the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
